    "created_at": "2016-06-02T07:57:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-02T07:57:48Z",
    "body": "When preparing a PR for this I noticed another thing that's different between setting `currentTime` and `fastSeek()`, namely that the `currentTime` setter says \"if the media element's `readyState` is `HAVE_NOTHING`, then it must set the media element's default playback start position to the new value\".\n\nThis was added to Blink in https://codereview.chromium.org/517593003 but it looks like it hasn't been implemented in WebKit yet.\n\nJer, assuming you want to eventually implement that, what do you think should be the behavior for `fastSeek()` when `readyState` is `HAVE_NOTHING`? The current spec silently does nothing at all, but the alternatives are:\n1. Set the default playback start position.\n2. Also add a flag saying that it should be a fast seek.\n\nSince WebKit has the only (right? I forget) implementation of `fastSeek()` the spec might just as well match what you intend to do, so WDYT?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
