    "created_at": "2016-06-02T08:34:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-02T08:34:29Z",
    "body": "Fun, fun, another difference between WebKit and Blink seems to be that Blink clamps the time to [0, duration] before setting `m_lastSeekTime`, while WebKit does not, and the spec agrees with WebKit. I've only looked at the code, no testing.\n\nI think that WebKit's behavior probably makes more sense, because this way you don't need to know anything about the state of the backend synchronously in the setter, but can just create a request that is put into a queue and handled in order.\n\nNote to self: ensure that this is tested in web-platform-tests.\n",
